s9-3-p74 = prose (cons "Let \(R_{\mathrm{val}}(d,v)\) relate a direct value representation \(d\) to an evaluator value representation \(v\), with type indices and any required heap ownership or aliasing conditions retained. For direct target states \(D\) and evaluator configurations \(V\), a crossing is justified by a relation \(\mathcal X:D\to V\to\mathcal U\) preserving the represented continuation, live values through \(R_{\mathrm{val}}\), outstanding requests, and its observations. A direct-to-evaluator transfer establishes \(R_V\) for the encoded configuration; an evaluator-to-direct transfer, when used, establishes the receiving block's value and state premises. The existence of \(R_{\mathrm{val}}\) does not follow merely from both representations containing a word with the same bits. A direct segment ending at \(d\) may continue through the evaluator at \(v\) when \(\mathcal X(d,v)\) holds; returning to direct code requires a further relation only if that return is actually performed. A complete mixed artifact is a composition of direct block proofs, crossing relations, and finite or guarded iterations of \(\nu\). Its correctness is their composite evidence, not a claim that a runtime boundary introduces a second semantics." nil)
